# Cross-platform UI parity (Mac = Windows)

Public UI must render and behave the same on Mac and Windows (Chrome/Edge). Prefer geometry that does not depend on overlay vs classic scrollbars or DPI quirks.

## Hard rules

1. **No `100vw` for full-bleed width** — use `width: 100%` / `w-full`. Classic Windows scrollbars make `100vw` overflow or crop.
2. **One viewport unit family per component** — do not mix `vh` with `dvh`/`svh` for the same measured box (e.g. panel + mask). Prefer `svh`/`dvh` for sticky pins and full-viewport sections.
3. **JS scrub must match CSS pin** — never drive sticky/parallax progress with bare `window.innerHeight` when CSS uses `100svh`. Use `measureStickyPinHeightPx` / `readStickyPinHeightPx` from `useStickyScrub.ts`, or measure the live `[data-sticky-pin]` element.
4. **One header offset token** — prefer `--site-header-height` (set by `SiteHeader`). Fall back to `--header-offset` only when needed; do not invent a third offset.
5. **`fill` images need a sized relative parent** — Next/Image `fill` and CMS `Media fill` must sit in `relative` + explicit height/`aspect-*`/`inset-0` frame. Pass explicit `sizes` (e.g. `100vw` for heroes).
6. **Avoid webkit-only layout** — scrollbar hiding needs both `scrollbar-width: none` and `::-webkit-scrollbar`. Do not rely on `-webkit-font-smoothing` for visual weight.

## When building sticky / scroll sections

- Mark the sticky pin with `data-sticky-pin`.
- Runway height and pin height must use the same unit (`svh`).
- Re-check after resize; assume Windows 125%/150% scaling exists.

## Pre-merge check (UI changes)

- [ ] No new `100vw` widths for layout shells
- [ ] No `innerHeight` vs `svh` mismatch in scroll math
- [ ] Images have aspect/min-height + `object-cover`/`contain` intentional
- [ ] Sticky sections use shared helpers from `useStickyScrub.ts`
